    "# The Great Retrofit \u2014 v2 Agent-Based Model\n",
    "\n",
    "**J M Applegate, Yudhanjaya Wijeratne** \u agent-based retrofit co-op simulation.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook contains the full upgraded codebase of v2 in more easily explorable fashion: heterogeneous households, buildings, cooperatives, banks, spatial neighbourhoods, bargaining, income processes, investors, demographics, depreciation and new construction. Each code block is documented below with its workings and behaviour. The final section runs the simulation and plots **every tracked quantity** against a **time axis measured in weeks**.\n",
    "\n",
    "## How the model works (high level)\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Buildings** need retrofitting. They move through states: `to_do` \u2192 `queued` \u2192 `in_progress` \u2192 `finished`.\n",
    "- **Households** (owners) request retrofits with probability `aspiration/100` per week.\n",
    "- **Co-ops** take on projects when they have budget; they charge `(1+surplus)\u00d7price`.\n",
    "- **Banks** may lend ~50% of project cost; co-ops must keep payment-to-income \u2264 30%.\n",
    "- Weekly cost = `retrofit_cost / retrofit_time` per active project.\n",
    "- Defaults, investors, births/deaths, depreciation and construction modify the stock over time.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
