    "## 9. Gini helper\n",
    "\n",
    "**Workings:** `gini_coefficient` sorts values and applies the standard formula, shifting to non-negative if needed (wealths can in principle be zero but not negative here; the shift is defensive). Returns 0 for empty or all-zero inputs.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def gini_coefficient(values: np.ndarray) -> float:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Calculate Gini coefficient of an array of values.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Handles negative values by shifting to non-negative.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    if len(values) == 0:\n",
    "        return 0.0\n",
    "    values = np.array(values)\n",
    "    min_val = np.min(values)\n",
    "    if min_val < 0:\n",
    "        values = values - min_val\n",
    "    values = np.sort(values)\n",
    "    n = len(values)\n",
    "    cumsum = np.cumsum(values)\n",
    "    if cumsum[-1] == 0:\n",
    "        return 0.0\n",
    "    return (2 * np.sum((np.arange(1, n+1) * values))) / (n * cumsum[-1]) - (n + 1) / n\n"
   ]
