    "## 10. Simulation engine (`run_simulation`)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Workings:** Orchestrates one full run week by week (`t` from 0 to `run_time-1`):\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Record** current counts, Gini (wealth + income sample), unemployment, queue waits, bank losses, per-neighbourhood queue.\n",
    "2. **Retrofit requests** \u2014 `to_do` buildings whose owner `wants_retrofit` move to `queued`.\n",
    "3. **Matching & bargaining** \u2014 for each queued building, sample `search_length` co-ops (or all), pick one with capacity; optionally negotiate price (bid vs reservation); request a bank loan for ~50% of projects.\n",
    "4. **Work** \u2014 co-ops pay weekly cost; on completion revenue `(1+surplus)\u00d7price` is booked and household wealth reduced by price.\n",
    "5. **Defaults** \u2014 banks check solvency, process defaults (50% recovery).\n",
    "6. **Income process** \u2014 AR(1) update.\n",
    "7. **Investors** \u2014 buy finished buildings when expected return > hurdle.\n",
    "8. **Demographics** \u2014 deaths (building \u2192 `to_do`), births (new households).\n",
    "9. **Depreciation** \u2014 condition decay.\n",
    "10. **Construction** \u2014 new buildings when avg finished price > 1.2\u00d7 build cost.\n",
    "\n",
    "Stops early if all `n` buildings finished (unless construction enabled). Returns a `Result` with trimmed arrays of length `actual_weeks`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Behaviour notes:** Recording happens at the *start* of each week before updates, so week 0 reflects initial state. Early-exit can make arrays shorter than `run_time+1`; `actual_weeks` tracks this.\n"
   ]
  },
